From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: smit1237 <smit1237@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 23:13:19 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 28/30] lan: one bridged LAN (br-lan) for USB-C and the WiFi
 hotspot

The USB-C NCM link and the W board's hotspot now share one LAN,
br-lan = 10.42.0.1/24, instead of a separate 192.168.42.0/24 hotspot
subnet.

- kernel: CONFIG_BRIDGE=y (plain L2 bridge; no bridge netfilter).
- S30gadget_nic creates br-lan at every boot (STP off, forward_delay 0,
  multicast snooping off, per-unit MAC), enslaves usb0 and puts the LAN
  address on the bridge; falls back to addressing usb0 directly if the
  bridge can't be made. The LAN iface in use is recorded in
  /run/lan-iface and read by every consumer.
- hostapd joins the AP iface to br-lan (bridge=br-lan); ap_ip/ap_dhcp_*
  are gone. dnsmasq serves one pool, 10.42.0.10-.250.
- Firewall (generated, early, fallback, emergency), IPv6 confinement and
  Reticulum's AutoInterface (devices = br-lan, usb0; bitrate pinned at
  10 Mbit/s) follow the LAN iface; the portal shows one LAN.
- Docs updated.
